 (status sourceUrl markdown)←FetchReadme(projectUrl version);urls;i;u;c;q;resp;answered;maxSize
⍝ Fetches a package's README from GitHub, keyed on the release's own tag. Returns one of:
⍝ * ('ok' sourceUrl markdown) - found
⍝ * ('none' '' '')            - GitHub answered and there is no README to be had
⍝ * ('error' '' '')           - GitHub could not be reached at all
⍝ The last two matter because only a settled answer is recorded (see `FetchAndStoreReadme`):
⍝ 'none' is a fact about the repository and stands, while 'error' says only that this
⍝ attempt failed, and writing it down as 'none' would bake a network hiccup into the
⍝ Registry for good.
⍝ Rumba is used rather than HttpCommand: HttpCommand belongs to the client, and although it
⍝ currently finds its way into the server workspace as well, that is an accident and no
⍝ foundation to build on. Rumba is already there on purpose - `CreateAllRefs` aliases it as
⍝ `R` - and its client side speaks TLS, which is all this needs.
⍝ Rumba reports a connection that failed by signalling 345 rather than by a return code, so
⍝ "GitHub answered" simply means a response came back at all. 345 is the only number it
⍝ uses for that - `CongaError` maps every Conga return code onto it - so that is all that is
⍝ trapped here, and anything else is a fault in this code and had better be seen.
⍝ A failed connection is not logged: it is recorded against the package as 'error' instead,
⍝ where it belongs, and logging every timeout would bury the log during a GitHub outage.
 (status sourceUrl markdown)←'error' '' ''
 answered←0
 maxSize←262144                                     ⍝ 256 KB; anything larger is not a README
 urls←GetReadmeUrls projectUrl version
 :If 0=≢urls
     status←'none'                                  ⍝ Nowhere to look is not a network problem
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :For i :In ⍳≢urls
     :Trap 345                                      ⍝ Rumba turns every failed connection into 345
         u←R.ParseURI i⊃urls[;1]
         c←R.NewClient u
         c.CongaTimeout←3000                        ⍝ Milliseconds; raw.githubusercontent is a CDN
         c.ClientTimeout←10                         ⍝ Seconds, for the exchange as a whole
         q←R.NewRequest u.Resource
         resp←⊃c R.SendAndReceive q
     :Else
         :Continue                                  ⍝ Signalled: timed out, closed, or no route
     :EndTrap
     answered←1
     :If 200=resp.StatusCode
     :AndIf 0<≢resp.Content
     :AndIf maxSize≥≢resp.Content
         (status sourceUrl markdown)←'ok'(i⊃urls[;2])resp.Content
         :Return
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
 :If answered
     status←'none'
 :EndIf
